From a0e8048909cd96c0b4028c51cb4f9b78eda960e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atchaya R <quic_ratchaya@quicinc.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Sep 2024 09:59:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] openwrt patches for opensync

Added support for user defnied multicast exceptions, which allows the user to
make the packets that match these exceptions always flood. This behaviour is
configurable through the OVS bridge other_config variable. IPv4 and IPv6 are
both supported. Note that IGMP and MLD are not subject to these exceptions.

IPv6 example: "ovs-vsctl set Bridge br-home \
	other_config:mcast-ipv6-exceptions=ff01::/16,ff02::5/128"
IPv4 example: "ovs-vsctl set Bridge br-home \
	other_config:mcast-ipv4-exceptions=1.1.1.1/8,192.168.25.0/24"

Signed-off-by: Atchaya R <quic_ratchaya@quicinc.com>

